    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern for `namesakeCount` (a point-in-time snapshot captured on create), I made these changes:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter and `toString` entry.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicService.java` + `ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `countHouseholdMembers(householdId)`, which counts stored owners sharing a household identifier (mirroring `countNamesakes`/`countOwnersInCity`).\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 after household assignment (which sets the `householdId` and back-fills existing members), the controller records the household size as the stored members under that `householdId` plus the new owner (or `1` for an owner that joins no household).\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `formatMembershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, falling through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic otherwise. Added `@Mapping(ignore)` for `householdSize` on both `toOwner` overloads since it isn't a request input.\n\n5. **Schema files** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD tier.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nNote: the working directory is not a git repository, so no commit was made \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one and commit.",
